      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T23:25:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this same CL, I am modifying the \"default\" policy, that is, the code usually called by `q-\u003epolicy-\u003eadd()` below.  Previously, that function would silently ignore being called with a zero count.  So I made the change here for the case that some existing callers would occasionally call `queue_advance_tail()` with a zero count, while relying on the consumer NOT being notified about that no-op.\n\nThe only place a policy other than the default (or the null policy) is used is in `common/usb_console_stream.c`, in which `console_has_input()` is invoked to wake up the console task whether the count is zero or non-zero.  But since the console task simply consumes one byte at a time, and is still woken up any time a non-zero count of characters are enqued, then it cannot have any effect to stop notifying about \"zero characters added\".\n\nBy the above reasoning, adding this condition is safe.  And it is necessary in order to ensure that zero-byte `add()` will only be called when an flush is explicitly requested.",
      "parentUuid": "808118eb_81e10d83",
      "revId": "014b04c3b006a3cdec86eec1f45410caf613dd1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
