      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T23:25:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have added a comment to this function, to explain the reasons and caveats.\n\nOrdinarily, I am all for descriptive names for contants.  But in this case, I wonder what I should do about code such as `if (transfer \u003e 0)`.  I am afraid that if people cannot immediately see that the value is zero, but just a constant name, that could cause confusion.  (Posix does not have a value for END_OF_STREAM that we check against the return value of `read()`, probably because having one would be confusing if readers cannot see that the named constant does not have a positive value.)\n\nLet me know if you still think that a constant is the best choice here.",
